      propertyPath: m_text
      value: '


        Real treasury paper has a watermark pressed into it. You
        only see it with special UV light. Fakes printed on new paper show nothing.
        But not all documents have a watermark, as you might expect.


        Read
        the text as well. Bogus documents get dates, names or titles wrong. Sometimes
        it difficult to resolve issue date, but it is probably the one that is printed. '
